<title>USA: TABLE - First Banks Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - First Banks Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except net income/loss per share)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					  June 30,	   June 30,</p>
<p>				 1997	 1996	1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net Interest Income  $3,841	$2,530    $7,381     $5,064</p>
<p>Provision for loan</p>
<p>   losses		    735	   250     1,285	  350</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	 796	   438     1,173	  899</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>  per share		  .22	   .11	 .32	  .23</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>shares and common share</p>
<p>equivalents outstanding</p>
<p>			     3,612	 3,973     3,644	3,990</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said results for Q2 and first-half 1997 reflect the impact of its acquisition of Sunrise Bank, completed in November 1996.</p>
<p>Results for the current three and six-month periods include about $297,000 and $573,000, respectively, of interest expense attributable to acquisition costs.</p>
<p>Full name is First Bank America Inc.</p>
